Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: segl
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/robert-patrick-texas/segl/issues
Source: https://github.com/robert-patrick-texas/segl
Comment:
 The package carries a Python runtime of its own under /opt/segl, and a web
 application built from npm packages. Each bundled part's full license text
 ships in the package. The paragraphs below say where.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 segl contributors
License: Apache-2.0

Files: opt/segl/python/*
Copyright: 2001-2026 Python Software Foundation and contributors
License: PSF-2.0
Comment:
 CPython, built by the python-build-standalone project
 (https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone). That build links
 several libraries into the interpreter, among them OpenSSL, SQLite, zlib,
 bzip2, xz, zstd, libffi, expat, ncurses, and mpdecimal, each under a
 permissive license of its own, as that project documents.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/fastapi* opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/annotated_doc*
Copyright: 2018 Sebastián Ramírez (fastapi); 2025 Sebastián Ramírez (annotated-doc)
License: MIT
Comment: fastapi, the web framework of the API, and annotated-doc. The full
 texts are in the fastapi-*.dist-info and annotated_doc-*.dist-info licenses
 folders.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/starlette* opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/uvicorn*
Copyright: 2018 Encode OSS Ltd (starlette); 2017-present Encode OSS Ltd (uvicorn)
License: BSD-3-Clause
Comment: starlette and uvicorn, the ASGI toolkit and server. The full texts
 are in the starlette-*.dist-info and uvicorn-*.dist-info licenses folders.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/websockets*
Copyright: Aymeric Augustin and contributors
License: BSD-3-Clause
Comment: websockets, the WebSocket protocol of the live boards. The full text
 is in the websockets-*.dist-info licenses folder.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/pydantic* opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/typing_inspection* opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/annotated_types*
Copyright: 2017 to present Pydantic Services Inc. and individual contributors (pydantic);
 2022 Samuel Colvin (pydantic-core);
 2025 to present Pydantic Services Inc. (typing-inspection);
 2022 the contributors (annotated-types)
License: MIT
Comment: pydantic, pydantic-core, typing-inspection, and annotated-types. The
 full texts are in their dist-info licenses folders.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/anyio*
Copyright: 2018 Alex Grönholm
License: MIT
Comment: anyio. The full text is in the anyio-*.dist-info licenses folder.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/h11*
Copyright: 2016 Nathaniel J. Smith and other contributors
License: MIT
Comment: h11, the HTTP/1.1 protocol uvicorn serves with. The full text is in
 the h11-*.dist-info licenses folder.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/click* opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/idna*
Copyright: 2014 Pallets (click); 2013-2026 Kim Davies and contributors (idna)
License: BSD-3-Clause
Comment: click and idna. The full texts are in the click-*.dist-info and
 idna-*.dist-info licenses folders.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/typing_extensions*
Copyright: Python Software Foundation and contributors
License: PSF-2.0
Comment: typing-extensions. The full text is in the
 typing_extensions-*.dist-info licenses folder.

Files: opt/segl/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/opentelemetry*
Copyright: The OpenTelemetry Authors
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: opentelemetry-api, which fastapi depends on. The full text is in the
 opentelemetry_api-*.dist-info licenses folder.

Files: opt/segl/app/web/dist/*
Copyright: 2026 segl contributors; and the authors of the bundled packages
License: Apache-2.0 and MIT and ISC and BSD-3-Clause and 0BSD and Zlib and CC0-1.0
Comment:
 The web application, built from web/ with Vite. Its minified files hold
 segl's own code (Apache-2.0) together with Excalidraw
 (@excalidraw/excalidraw, MIT), React, React Router, and the npm packages
 those depend on. /usr/share/doc/segl/web-licenses/PACKAGES.txt lists every
 bundled package with its version and license. Each package's license text,
 with its copyright notice, is in a folder beside that list, named after the
 package and its version. Where a package offers a choice of licenses, segl
 takes the one in the License field above. The package build fails when a
 bundled package has no license text (web/scripts/collect-licenses.ts).

Files: opt/segl/app/web/dist/fonts/* opt/segl/app/web/dist/assets/*.woff2
Copyright: The authors of each font, as its folder under
 /usr/share/doc/segl/font-licenses/ names them
License: OFL-1.1 and MIT
Comment:
 The fonts of the Excalidraw editor. /usr/share/doc/segl/font-licenses/ has
 a folder for each, with its copyright notice and its license text.
 .
 OFL-1.1: Assistant, Cascadia, Excalifont, Liberation, Lilita, Nunito,
 Virgil, Xiaolai.
 MIT: ComicShanns.
 .
 All are the files @excalidraw/excalidraw ships, but for Liberation. That
 package ships Liberation Sans 1.05, which is under the GNU General Public
 License. segl does not ship that file. It ships Liberation Sans 2.1.5 in
 its place, from https://github.com/liberationfonts/liberation-fonts, under
 the SIL Open Font License.

License: Apache-2.0
 On Debian systems, the full text of the Apache License 2.0 is in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0. The package also carries it as
 /usr/share/doc/segl/LICENSE.

